{%- doc -%}
  Recursively renders one tier of a Shopify navigation menu for the
  category mega menu. Depth 1 links are styled as column headers; deeper
  ones are plain leaf links.

  Migrated from the old `menu_node` metaobject tree (2026-08-20). The
  three lower tiers of the mega menu are now real Shopify menus, one per
  menu_group, so the client can restructure them in Online Store →
  Navigation without touching metaobjects. Only the top tier (the
  Consumabile / Echipamente / Piese de schimb headings) is still a
  metaobject — see sections/dalbe-category-nav.liquid.

  A Shopify menu allows at most 3 nested levels
  (https://shopify.dev/docs/api/liquid/objects/linklist — `levels`), which
  is exactly why the split lands here: those 3 levels fit one menu, the
  4th (the group heading) cannot.

  @param {array} links - `linklist.links`, or a parent link's `.links`
  @param {number} [depth] - Recursion depth. Starts at 1 for the tier directly under a category.

  @example
  {% render 'dalbe-category-nav-list', links: category.links %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{% liquid
  assign depth = depth | default: 1
%}
<ul class="dalbe-category-nav__node-list list-unstyled" data-depth="{{ depth }}">
  {% for link in links %}
    {% liquid
      assign child_links = link.links
      assign next_depth = depth | plus: 1
    %}
    <li class="dalbe-category-nav__node dalbe-category-nav__node--depth-{{ depth }}">
      <a
        href="{{ link.url }}"
        class="dalbe-category-nav__node-link"
      >
        {{ link.title }}
      </a>
      {% if child_links.size > 0 %}
        {% render 'dalbe-category-nav-list', links: child_links, depth: next_depth %}
      {% endif %}
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
